# Code owners for runward.
# Every change requests a review from the maintainer by default.
# See GOVERNANCE.md for the decision model.
* @stranxik

# ADR-0088 (decisions 5 and 7): the delegation charter, the lock's opt-ins, the forge configuration
# and the gate-critical paths whose changes wait for the maintainer before merge. Today every line
# below names the same owner as `*` above, so they change no review request; they are written out so
# the trust-root paths stay the maintainer's when `*` gains another owner (the last matching pattern
# wins), and so the pre-merge list can be read where the forge applies it.
#
# What this does and does not guard, stage 1. A code owner is a user or a team with write access,
# never an App: with "Require review from Code Owners" on, a pull request touching these paths needs
# an approval from @stranxik, and an approval by runward-steward[bot] does not count as one (by the
# documentation; not yet measured, ADR-0088 "What would settle it"). The maintainer cannot approve a
# pull request the maintainer's own account opened. While agent sessions hold the maintainer's
# credential, an agent can give that approval, or change this file and the branch rules: the guard
# binds delegate identities, not an agent acting as the maintainer. Turning code-owner review on is an
# administrator's act and is not done by this file.
